  "summary": {
    "en": "Pachycephalosaurus had a thick, dome-shaped skull roof ringed with bony knobs. It walked on two legs and lived in western North America at the very end of the Cretaceous. Most fossils are skulls, so the rest of its body is poorly known."
  },
